# Copy to .env. Never commit .env.
#
# EVERYTHING in this file ends up in the browser bundle, readable by anyone who
# opens the site. No password, token or secret key belongs here, ever — and not
# written into web/src either. The old build shipped a shared login password
# that way.
#
# The API needs no setting: /api is proxied to http://localhost:4000 in
# development (vite.config.js) and served from the same domain in production.

# Only until Day 19, for the parts still read from Supabase: payroll history,
# reports, documents, notifications and bank details.
# The ANON key from Supabase -> Project Settings -> API. It is public by design;
# the service_role key must never go here.
# Left empty: `npm run dev` shows demo rows kept in the browser, and a production
# build says those parts cannot load instead of showing made-up data.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
